# the same three with the collector compiled in -- `make asan`/`ubsan`/`tsan` build both
ziman-asan-gc
ziman-ubsan-gc
ziman-tsan-gc
ziman-vg
third_party/
vendor/bdwgc/gc.o
vendor/bdwgc/libgc.a
vendor/bdwgc/libgc-tsan.a
# Every build artefact now lands under build/ (objects, .d files and the generated *_source.h
# headers); the bare *.o/*.d stay for the C unit tests, which build straight into /tmp but may be
# compiled by hand beside their source.
build/
*.o
*.d
# Kept after the 2026-10-14 move of generated headers into build/: a tree built before it still has
# these beside the sources, and `#include "json_source.h"` is a quoted include, so the compiler
# would prefer the stale copy next to corelib.c over the fresh one in build/. `make clean` deletes
# them; this keeps them from showing up as untracked until someone does.
src/*_source.h
tests/integration/pg/.url
tests/integration/tls/.certs/
tests/integration/pg/.certs/
editors/vscode/node_modules/

# Log files the sample backend writes, relative to wherever it is run from
# (application.properties: logging.file=logs/health-record.log), plus log.zm's
# rotated `.1`, `.2`, ... siblings. The directory itself stays tracked, through
# logs/.gitkeep: fs.append_text does not create a missing directory, it just
# fails, so a fresh clone without logs/ would silently stop logging.
logs/*.log
logs/*.log.*

# tools/preflight.sh writes one log per step
.preflight-*.log

# Claude Code session state: a lock file for scheduled tasks and any throwaway
# worktrees. The skills under .claude/skills/ are committed on purpose -- they are
# repository tooling -- so this ignores the state beside them rather than the directory.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/

# npx wrangler writes here when deploying websites/ (see websites/README.md)
.wrangler/

# drawn by tools/gen_lib_map.py at publish time, never committed
websites/ziman.dev/library-map.html
